<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Renaissance of the 12th century</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as twelfth-century Renaissance</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a> of the 12th century was a period of intellectual revival in western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a> marked by the recovery of Greek and Arabic learning, the growth of cathedral schools and the rise of the first universities. It built on the classical <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/latin">Latin</a> texts preserved and copied during the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-renaissance">Carolingian Renaissance</a>. The site's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/carolingian-empire">Carolingian Empire</a> profile presents that earlier scribal tradition as the bridge to this later revival.</p></div>
